  "detail": null,
  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 13 members) worked per RBC-QM-02. Measurement period: CY2026; ages as of 2026-12-31. I checked the full procedure, condition, care-episode, order and note records for each member, plus coded stool tests, colonoscopy, sigmoidoscopy and CT colonography across the clinic. No member had an active FIT order before today.\n\nFor each open gap I placed one mailed FIT kit order (LAB-FIT-KIT, window 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31) and sent the patient a message. The message says the kit is on its way and explains how to collect the sample and mail it back by 12/31/2026. Patients without an open gap got no order and no contact.\n\n| Patient | Age | Status | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow | 72 | Excluded | 66 or older, has active frailty (since 2025-09) and is taking donepezil, a dementia medication (active order from 2025-06) |\n| pt-0011 Marilu Gaona | 62 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0001), message sent | No qualifying screening on record. Her hospice episode ended 2025-10-20, before 2026, so it does not exclude her |\n| pt-0014 Santo Pagac | 55 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0002), message sent | No screening done. The 2026 colonoscopy order (sr-00002) is still active but was never done; he did not show for the 4/14 appointment. An order or appointment does not count |\n| pt-0018 Lance Muller | 53 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0003), message sent | His stool DNA-FIT sample was collected 2023-12-27, outside the 2024–2026 window (resulted 2024-01-08, but collection date counts). His FIT from 2021 is too old |\n| pt-0019 Harrison O'Keefe | 69 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0004), message sent | No screening. He has active frailty but no advanced illness: donepezil was stopped 2023-03-20 (testing showed mild cognitive impairment, not dementia). He lives at home |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan | 52 | Excluded | Hospice episode 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21 (pancreatic cancer) |\n| pt-0021 Ángela Vigil | 52 | Excluded | Total proctocolectomy in 2015, found in a scanned outside operative report |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss | 52 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0005), message sent | Her FIT sample was collected 2025-12-29, before 2026 (resulted 2026-01-05, but collection date counts) |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0006), message sent | Her last stool test was 2024-06-11, not in 2026. The 2025 colonoscopy order (sr-00003) was never done |\n| pt-0034 Rickey Sipes | 72 | Excluded | 66 or older and lives long term in a nursing home: his home address is Maple Grove Care Center, Room 214, with nursing-facility visits in 2/2026 and 7/2026 |\n| pt-0035 Elvin Wolff | 68 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0007), message sent | No screening. His skilled-nursing stay (5/3–5/24/2026) was short-term rehab after hip surgery and he went home. No frailty, advanced illness or hospice |\n| pt-0036 Nick Bartoletti | 53 | Open gap: FIT ordered (sr-t0008), message sent | No screening. His 2021 sigmoid colectomy removed only part of the colon, which does not exclude |\n| pt-0037 Fumiko Pouros | 35 | Not in population | Below the age range (46–75) |\n\nTotals: 8 open gaps (8 FIT orders, 8 patient messages), 4 excluded, 1 not in the population, 0 already up to date.\n\nFollow-up for you: the colonoscopy orders for pt-0014 (sr-00002) and pt-0024 (sr-00003) are still active even though their dates have passed. I left them unchanged.",
